.TH NOTHOS 1 "October 2026" "Nothos V18.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nothos \- Ancient Greek philology, lexicons, and primary-source research
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nothos research
.RI "\"" query "\""
.RB [ --sources " " lsj,galen,pgm,lxx ]
.RB [ --related ]
.RB [ --all ]
.RB [ --top-k " " N ]
.RB [ --no-ai ]
.RB [ --model " " MODEL ]
.RB [ --output " " PATH ]
.br
.B nothos etymology
.RI "\"" word "\""
.RB [ --variants ]
.RB [ --ai ]
.RB [ --model " " MODEL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Nothos combines local LSJ lexical evidence, optional FAISS related-headword
retrieval, and Greek primary texts including locally indexed Galen, Greek
magical papyri, and the Septuagint (LXX). Optional Ollama analysis is generated
commentary and must be checked against the original Greek.
.PP
Available options and commands depend on the version installed locally.
.SH WORDS TO SEARCH
.TP
.B λίβανος (libanos)
Frankincense, the aromatic resin. Search as written and review related forms.
.TP
.B λιβανωτός (libanotos)
A distinct incense/frankincense term worth searching separately.
.TP
.B σμύρνα (smyrna)
Myrrh, the aromatic resin. This may also overlap spelling used for Smyrna,
the city; verify context in each passage.
.TP
.B σμύρνη (smyrne)
Alternative Greek spelling to examine independently; verify corpus entries.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Evidence-only frankincense across primary sources
.nf
nothos research "λίβανος" --sources lsj,galen,pgm,lxx --all --no-ai
.fi
.SS Evidence-only myrrh across primary sources
.nf
nothos research "σμύρνα" --sources lsj,galen,pgm,lxx --all --no-ai
.fi
.SS Related LSJ candidate spellings (not proven etymologies)
.nf
nothos research "λίβανος" --sources lsj,galen,pgm,lxx --related --top-k 10 --no-ai
nothos research "σμύρνα" --sources lsj,galen,pgm,lxx --related --all --no-ai
.fi
.SS Search incense-related word forms independently
.nf
nothos research "λιβανωτός" --sources lsj,galen,pgm,lxx --all --no-ai
nothos research "σμύρνη" --sources lsj,galen,pgm,lxx --all --no-ai
.fi
.SS Compare frankincense and myrrh with local Ollama
.nf
nothos research "λίβανος" --sources lsj,galen,pgm,lxx --top-k 8 --model gemma3:4b
nothos research "σμύρνα" --sources lsj,galen,pgm,lxx --top-k 8 --model gemma3:4b
.fi
.SS Etymology workflow, when available
.nf
nothos etymology "λίβανος" --variants --ai --model gemma3:4b --color always
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --sources lsj,galen,pgm,lxx
Select indexed collections. Availability depends on your local installation.
.TP
.B --related
Look for related LSJ spellings in selected sources; not historical proof.
.TP
.B --all
Return all matching Temple passages; may produce extensive output.
.TP
.B --top-k N
Limit retrieved results when not using --all.
.TP
.B --no-ai
Skip generated analysis and show retrieval evidence.
.TP
.B --model MODEL
Select an available Ollama model for AI synthesis.
.TP
.B --output PATH
Write a report to a UTF-8 file when supported.
.SH NOTES
The labels LSJ, Galen, PGM, and LXX describe separate sources. A zero-result
search does not establish that a word is unattested in all ancient literature.
Greek accents, inflected forms, corpus editions, and OCR may affect matching.
LSJ headword similarity is not proof of common derivation.
